    "moreThanCurrentBestView": "It supplies an explicit exact-geometry data model that binds regions, shells, faces, loops, edgeuses, edges and vertices to analytic or NURBS geometry, while its official viewing paths separately tessellate those exact BReps into transient Hydra meshes or authored UsdGeomMesh prims. Current KAOPU already separates evidence layers in principle, but the N218/N219 mechanical receipt did not yet make authoring representation and runtime evaluation route independently auditable.",
    "reproducibilityEvidence": [
      "Public C++ and Python APIs",
      "Runnable examples",
      "Source build and full-test instructions",
      "BrepArray schema validator",
      "Kernel-backed geometry validator / AssertValid",
      "Public issue reproductions with exact versions and numeric expectations"
    ],
    "integrationRisks": [
      "The library's documented Hydra and PyVista viewing paths tessellate exact BReps into triangle meshes; exact source geometry cannot be used as evidence of a triangle-free display/runtime route.",
      "The kernel/OpenUSD toolchain is substantially heavier than the current WebGPU runtime and is not a direct browser dependency.",
      "macOS support is limited; the supported Python wheel targets CPython 3.12 on Linux and Windows.",
      "Known issues include malformed-data crashes, heal operations that can report success despite repair failure, and current 1.0.1 operations that can return success with invalid or semantically wrong output."
    ],
    "learningScope": "Learn the exact surface/topology schema, validation layering, operation postconditions, and the explicit authoring/display separation. Do not adopt tessellation, polygon display, STEP/USD production dependency, or the kernel as a global runtime; do not credit a renderer route as triangle-free without a separately bound evaluation trace."
  },
