      "CTS canvas_complex reftest with ComputeWorkgroup1x1TextureStore and ComputeWorkgroup16x16TextureStore",
      "CTS primitive-topology coverage"
    ],
    "integrationRisks": [
      "The direct storage-canvas route depends on the canvas format's STORAGE_BINDING capability; bgra8unorm requires bgra8unorm-storage while rgba8unorm supports write-only storage.",
      "A hidden fullscreen render/composite pass would reintroduce triangle primitives even if the main surface work happens in compute.",
      "The standards route proves command-path feasibility, not acceptable performance, numerical robustness, lighting correctness or the user's no-per-object-ray requirement.",
      "Browser, adapter, operating-system and physical-device support must be verified on the exact production subject."
    ],
    "learningScope": "Use compute dispatch plus storage-canvas presentation as the first triangle-free backend audition route. Do not claim the full function renderer is solved until the exact browser/device command trace and rendered result pass independently."
  },
  "currentBestViewComparison": {
    "existingCoverage": [
      "N218 already rejects surface-family labels, untrimmed quadrics, missing patch adjacency, C0/G1/G2 breaks, and missing reference-section residuals.",
      "R2 already requires independent verification and forbids Producer self-approval."
    ],
    "newDiscriminator": "WebGPU render and compute pipelines are materially different evidence routes. The render pipeline constructs only point, line or triangle primitives; an official CTS route writes the canvas current texture from a compute shader through STORAGE_BINDING and dispatchWorkgroups. A triangle-free backend claim must therefore bind every command encoder, pipeline kind, render draw count, primitive topology, compute dispatch and canvas usage/format capability."
  },
